hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24226","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn Rashid al-Zawfi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Murrah al-Zawfi, from Kharijah ibn Hudhafah al-Adawi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one morning and said: Allah has reinforced you with a prayer which is better for you than red camels. We said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Al-Witr, between the Isha prayer and the rising of dawn."
"24227","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn Rashid al-Zawfi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Murrah al-Zawfi, from Kharijah ibn Hudhafah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Allah has reinforced you with a prayer which is better for you than red camels; Allah has made it for you between the Isha prayer and the rising of dawn."
"24228","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Rashid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Murrah, a man from his people, from Kharijah ibn Hudhafah al-Qurashi, then one of Banu Adi ibn Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us for the dawn prayer and said: Allah has reinforced you tonight with a prayer which is better for you than red camels. He said: So I said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Al-Witr, between the Isha prayer and the rising of dawn."
